.gradle/
build/
*/build/
*/*/build/
local.properties
.idea/
*.iml
.kotlin/
.DS_Store

# Model weights (§7.3). Multi-GB GGUF files are fetched by tools/fetch-model.sh,
# never committed — a repo an examiner can clone in under a minute matters more
# than one that is self-contained.
models/
*.gguf

# llama.cpp is a submodule at third_party/llama.cpp (see .gitmodules), so it is
# tracked, not ignored. Only the host build output of the grammar checker is.
tools/gbnf-check/build/

# Generated evaluation output (§14). Results are reproduced by running the
# harness; committing them would let a stale table outlive the code that made it.
#
# That argument holds for the JVM harness and fails for the phone, which is the
# same split :bench's build file already draws: deterministic components run in
# CI on any machine, device-bound numbers do not. A run like E4b (hours, chunked
# around process kills, at one battery level) or E6b (memory sampled through a
# live planning run) cannot be reproduced by re-running anything — it is raw
# evidence, it is cited by name in docs/EXPERIMENTS.md, and a citation to a file
# that is not in the repository is not provenance.
#
# So the raw artefacts are tracked (28 KB, all of them) and the *derived* tables
# are not, which keeps the original objection satisfied: nothing here can outlive
# the code, because nothing here is generated by the code.
bench/results/**/derived/
bench/results/*.html
